  "name": "no zugzwang",
  "summary": [
    "Chess where you may pass instead of moving, unless you are in check.",
    "No one can be forced to move into a worse position, and no one is ever stalemated.",
    "Otherwise it is chess."
  ],
  "description": "Chess with one rule added: on your turn you may pass instead of moving, as long as you are not in check. Much of chess's endgame rests on zugzwang, the position where any move makes things worse and the player would rather not move at all; here they need not, so every king-and-pawn ending that turned on who had to move plays differently, and stalemate cannot happen. It is the pass on its own, measured beside chess to see how much of the game depended on having to move.",
